{"id":"wikibooks:cherry-brownies","verdict":"keep","recipes":[{"source":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook%3ACherry_Brownies","status":"fixed","reason":"decode fraction and temperature entities; retain base and topping ingredient context","ingredients":["Base: 2 ea. (100 g) eggs","Base: 1 cup (2.4 dl) white granulated sugar","Base: 6 tbsp margarine","Base: ¼ cup (0.6 dl) cocoa","Base: ¾ cup (1.8 dl) flour","Base: ¼ tsp salt","Topping: 4 ounces (110 g) softened cream cheese","Topping: ¼ cup (0.6 dl) maraschino cherry syrup","Topping: ¼ cup (0.6 dl) icing sugar","Topping: 1 egg","Topping: ½ cup (1.2 dl) semi-sweet chocolate chips","Topping: ½ cup (1.2 dl) maraschino cherries"],"steps":["Melt margarine in a saucepan over medium-low heat, then mix in the cocoa.","Add the base sugar, salt, and eggs. Mix well and then fold in the flour.","Spread in a greased 9 x 9-inch (22 x 22 cm) cake pan and set aside.","Beat the cream cheese, cherry syrup and icing sugar together in a bowl until creamy.","Add the topping egg to the mixture and blend well.","Mix in the chocolate chips and cherries.","Pour the second mixture over top the base.","Bake at 350 °F/175 °C for 30–40 minutes, until a toothpick poked through the centre comes out moist (but not wet with batter).","Let cool and cut into 36 squares."]}]}
